<Layout
  title="Stage Screen privacy policy"
  description="What the Stage Screen iPhone and iPad app collects (anonymous usage statistics via PostHog), what it doesn't, and how to get in touch."
>
  <h2>Stage Screen privacy policy</h2>
  <p><em>Last updated 11 October 2026.</em></p>
  <p>
    Stage Screen is a countdown timer for iPhone and iPad that shows the timer on an
    external display. It is made by Bence Nagy.
  </p>

  <h3>What the app collects</h3>
  <p>
    The app has no accounts and asks for nothing about you. It does send anonymous
    usage data to PostHog, an analytics service, so I can see whether the app is used
    and whether the external display feature works for people:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Usage events</strong>, such as the app being opened, a timer being
      started, which screens are viewed, and whether a display was connected (and
      whether it was a mirrored external screen or an app window). Timer durations are
      included; the text of messages you type is not.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A random device identifier</strong> generated by the analytics library,
      plus basic device information: device model, iOS version, app version, and the
      country derived from your IP address when the data is sent.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This data is not linked to your name, email or any account. It is not used for
    advertising, not shared with anyone for advertising, and not used to track you
    across other apps or websites.
  </p>

  <h3>Where it goes</h3>
  <p>
    Usage data is sent to <a href="https://posthog.com">PostHog</a> (PostHog Inc.),
    which stores it on my behalf. PostHog's own privacy policy is at{" "}
    <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy">posthog.com/privacy</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>What the app does not collect</h3>
  <p>
    No location, contacts, photos, microphone or camera access. No crash reports
    beyond what Apple shares with developers under your own iOS settings. Timer
    settings and messages stay on your device.
  </p>

  <h3>Your choices</h3>
  <p>
    If you would rather not send usage data, the only option today is not to use the
    app; there is no in-app switch yet. If you want data associated with your device
    deleted, write to me and I will do it.
  </p>

  <h3>Contact</h3>
  <p>
    Bence Nagy, <a href="mailto:stagescreen@bence.dev">stagescreen@bence.dev</a>
  </p>
</Layout>
